# Summary of changes for run 3000f4c6-b78a-4a3f-aa78-96788a67cd58
## What was produced

Five new, mutually dependent Lean 4 files in `Catalog/Shared/`, all building against the project's mathlib with **zero sorries** and only the standard axioms (`propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`), plus `ComputationalEvidence.md`, `FUTURE_DIRECTIONS.md` and `SELF_EVALUATION.json` at the project root.

**`SpeculativeDecodingCostDominance.lean`** — the block model `speedup a c d = (∑_{i≤d} aⁱ)/(1 + c·d)`:
- exact head-to-head criterion, and the cheap-draft law at equal acceptance;
- `cost_dominance_all_six`: fed the measured acceptances and relative draft costs, the 0.5B draft beats the 1.5B draft in all six cells, including the one where the 1.5B accepts more;
- `tendsto_d_speedup` / `asymptotic_cost_dominance`: `d·speedup → 1/(c(1−a))`, so the ranking invariant at depth is `c·(1−a)`; the expensive draft would need ≥77.8% acceptance to overturn it;
- `exists_depth_collapse` with an explicit gate, instantiated to the measured prose d=8 losses and the code d=8 win;
- `depth_frontier_monotone`: the "deepening pays" frontier is monotone in acceptance (proved by a termwise cross-multiplication over a product of sums) — the formal content of domain-parameterized depth;
- `iid_cannot_explain_code_depth8`: an informative failure — no per-position acceptance ≤ 0.8 makes d=8 beat d=4 at the small draft's cost, so the reported percentages are mean accepted fractions, not per-position probabilities;
- `verification_overhead_bracket`: under the mean-yield reading, reproducing both depth-8 signs forces the CPU verification pass to charge 0.19–0.44 target-steps per extra position.

**`SpeculativeDecodingDepthUnimodality.lean`** — throughput is unimodal in depth for any concave yield over affine cost, so greedy depth tuning is exact (`greedy_depth_optimal`); the measured optima split strictly (prose 2, code 3).

**`SpeculativeDecodingAcceptanceProfiles.lean`** — per-position survival profiles: the averaging law (reported acceptance is automatically antitone in depth, so its measured decay is not evidence of drafter degradation), exact reconstruction of all six measured acceptance percentages by explicit monotone profiles, an unrealisability test with teeth, and the exact local stopping rule "deepen while next-position survival exceeds `c ×` current speedup".

**`SpeculativeDecodingCostCurve.lean`** — one strictly convex CPU cost curve with fixed per-block overhead, calibrated on three cells, reproduces all twelve measured speedups within 11% (nine out-of-sample); `no_affine_cost_curve_fits_code_cells` proves the curvature is forced by the data.

**`SpeculativeDecodingStopDepth.lean`** — the canonical stopping-depth selector: well defined, globally optimal, and monotone in acceptance; prose → 2, code → 3.

## Honest limits recorded in the files

The i.i.d. block model reproduces the win/loss sign of 11 of 12 measured cells and the winner of all 6 head-to-heads; the single failure is isolated and explained by a theorem rather than patched. The profile reconstruction is existence, not identification (only three partial sums per domain are pinned). Numeric cells are always stated as corollaries of quantified lemmas, never as standalone arithmetic.
